From: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 14:08:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net/handshake: do not send request when the socket is closed
References: bsc#1251942
Patch-Mainline: never, SLE15-SP7 specific

When the socket is closed we really should not send a handshake
request as the tlshd daemon has no way of acting sensibly on
the request. Better to error out request submission and let the
submitter deal with the error.

Upstream has solved this problem differently with the patchset
from Chunk Lever (https://lore.kernel.org/kernel-tls-handshake/20260525-handshake-file-pin-v3-0-66c616906ead@oracle.com/), but this would break the kABI for
SLE15 SP7. So we'll go with this simpler version instead which
already had been tested by the customer.

Signed-off-by: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
---
 net/handshake/request.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/handshake/request.c b/net/handshake/request.c
index 2829adbeb149..04a9e4f836df 100644
--- a/net/handshake/request.c
+++ b/net/handshake/request.c
@@ -236,6 +236,14 @@ int handshake_req_submit(struct socket *sock, struct handshake_req *req,
 		kfree(req);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
+	/* Prevent socket release while a handshake request is pending */
+	sock_hold(req->hr_sk);
+
+	if (req->hr_sk->sk_shutdown) {
+		sock_put(req->hr_sk);
+		kfree(req);
+		return -ESHUTDOWN;
+	}
 	req->hr_odestruct = req->hr_sk->sk_destruct;
 	req->hr_sk->sk_destruct = handshake_sk_destruct;
 	req->hr_file = sock->file;
@@ -267,9 +275,6 @@ int handshake_req_submit(struct socket *sock, struct handshake_req *req,
 			goto out_err;
 	}
 
-	/* Prevent socket release while a handshake request is pending */
-	sock_hold(req->hr_sk);
-
 	trace_handshake_submit(net, req, req->hr_sk);
 	return 0;
 
@@ -279,6 +284,7 @@ int handshake_req_submit(struct socket *sock, struct handshake_req *req,
 	/* Restore original destructor so socket teardown still runs on failure */
 	req->hr_sk->sk_destruct = req->hr_odestruct;
 	trace_handshake_submit_err(net, req, req->hr_sk, ret);
+	sock_put(req->hr_sk);
 	handshake_req_destroy(req);
 	return ret;
 }
